A||||14||ChadMan||My First Autocross  (Subtitle:  A Lesson in Humility)||||6||
Z||000000||ChadMan||04-22-2001||07:29 PM||||I raced in my first Solo II event today, in the 88 Coupe.  They put me in C Stock by mistake (s/b E Stock), so I was running against three 1st-gen MR2's and four other guys.  The MR2 guys were really cool (though of course they had to bust my balls a little about Fieros, naturally).<P>My first run was lousy, but I shaved 1.5 sec off my time over the course of the day.  The class leader had a lot of experience and was running Toyo racing tires on his MR2...he was about 4 sec quicker than me.  But the slowest MR2 was on street tires and we had a great duel going all day...I'd beat his best time, then he'd beat mine, back and forth until he finally made a great run and beat me by almost half a second.  I wound up finishing dead last in my class.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Oh well...maybe I'll do better next time.  Eric and rogergarrison, it was good to see you guys.||||reg||6
Z||000001||Eric||04-23-2001||12:46 AM||||I think you may be hooked now, Chadman.  Did you ever check out the times the guys in E stock were running?  <P>Next time I'll be there with my car, and we'll see how well the two 88's stack up against eachother.  From what I saw today, it may be quite a contest. <P>Roger seemed kind of excited by the prospect of coming back and running his Ferrari.  And I think Taijiguy wants to race once his car's sorted out.  We'll have a regular Fiero autocross club before you know it.  ||||reg||14
Z||000002||87ECO5||04-23-2001||08:56 AM||||Congrats and way to go, ChadMan!  Looking forward to hearing details this Friday!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Taijiguy||04-23-2001||09:17 AM||||GRRRRRRRRRRRRR!!!!!!  Stupid flywheel!!!!!<P>Instead of spending the day crushing pylons I spent the day crushing my knuckles. <IMG SRC="http://members.core.com/~taijiguy/simpsons.gif"> <P>Oh well, upside, I found the rear control arm bushings to be completely wasted (a good 1/4" minimum back and forth slop in the arm) So after I swap out the bushings it'll be tighter for next time! Look out guys, the beast is a-comin'!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric||04-23-2001||11:04 AM||||May 5 is the next event.  Well it's not an event really just a test and tune session.  May 6 is the driver's school.  They'll hook you up with an instructor and he or she will drive your car for a lap or two with you riding so you can get an impression on how it should be done.  If you want, you can just run your car without having to deal with an instructor.  It's fun either way.  Or you can let me drive you around since I'm like the guru of Fiero autocross  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>So I expect to see some of you guys on that weekend.  We'll have fun and eat doughnuts.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Taijiguy||04-23-2001||05:26 PM||||MMmmmmm....doughnuts  <IMG SRC="http://members.core.com/~taijiguy/miss13.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||firstfiero||04-23-2001||06:12 PM||||Man I wish I could autocross here in Pa. ....nothing going on aroung here anymore .<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif"> <BR>Todd <BR>  86se||||reg||1
Z||000007||Eric||04-23-2001||09:24 PM||||You're always welcome in our club if you can make the trip someday.<P>You know it would be too cool if we could organize an Ohio Fiero club founded around autocrossing.  There has to be some kind of and abandoned parking lot or airport that would let ~12 cars run for an afternoon.  We would have to find some cones though.  Fortunatly we live in a state that has a lot of road contruction going on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> so that wouldn't be too big of a problem.  With practice we all could be good enough to beat Phil and his blue MR2.  What do you say?||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||04-23-2001||09:31 PM||||I ended up going to plain city, delaware and buckeye lake, then went home to do the spring oil n filter change. Nice seeing you eric and chad. Maybe next time Ill leave all my junk at home and give it a shot.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||04-23-2001||09:33 PM||||I would love the opportunity to autocross my SE, its got a nice strong engine and 4-speed, but needs a little suspension work to make it somewhat competitive(shocks/struts). Shouldn't be too hard to find a nice open place for racing around here...don't have any place in mind though.||||reg||1
