Z||000011||Shaft||04-23-2001||09:53 PM||||Where on Fisher Rd. is the Delphi plant. I was drivin around on Sun. and tried to find it, but didn't see it on the part I was on.||||reg||1
Z||000012||ChadMan||04-24-2001||08:37 AM||||Shaft, the Delphi plant is actually at the corner of Georgesville Rd and Broad St.  The address is 200 Georgesville, but the entrance to the auto-x is on Broad (the first driveway east of Georgesville).<P>I am going to run on the bald Eagle ST's next time and see if I do better or worse.<P>I was thinking of how I could improve my times...sounds like a good idea for a new thread...||||reg||1
Z||000013||Taijiguy||04-24-2001||08:53 AM||||I'd be up for a club based on Autocrosses, and maybe we could throw in rallies as well. I'd be more than happy to help facilitate such a group. I'll even take the first step by starting a charter of potential members. Anyone interested in this can email me with your particulars. <BR>I know of a few places we could run. There's an old race track up in Powell, there's two shopping centers up on the northeast side (Cleveland and 161 that are almost always empty I'm sure we could contact the owners and get permission. We can rent cones and timing equipment. We would just probably need event insurance, anything else anyone can think of? <BR>Eric, let's get in touch about this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000014||Eric||04-24-2001||08:11 PM||||That's the main reason I never bothered to join COFE; they just don't do enough activities as a group.  I know there are a ton of sports car clubs that rent out tracks and have their own autocrosses.  I don't see any reason we couldn't do the same if we had enough "members" to our club.  If the logistics don't make it impossible, I think we could find enough members by next summer to make this thing work.  Maybe we could have some rallies this year because they're free and insurance is not an issue.||||reg||1
